# GOLDEN INTERVIEW ANSWERS

### List

> A List is an ordered and mutable collection of comma-separated elements enclosed within square brackets `[]`.

### Tuple

> A Tuple is an ordered and immutable collection of comma-separated elements enclosed within parentheses `()`.

### Set

> A Set is an unordered and mutable collection of unique elements enclosed within curly brackets `{}`.

### String

> A String is an immutable sequence of characters enclosed within single, double, or triple quotes.

### Indexing

> Indexing is the process of accessing an individual element using its position.

### Slicing

> Slicing is the process of extracting a portion of a sequence using `start`, `stop`, and `step`.

### Packing

> Packing means combining multiple values into a single tuple.

### Unpacking

> Unpacking means assigning the elements of a collection to separate variables.


